{"seq":2,"slug":"the-street-philosopher","title":"The Street Philosopher","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/life-and-times/the-street-philosopher","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-agora-and-dialogue","title":"广场与对话","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/life-and-times/the-street-philosopher/the-agora-and-dialogue","wordCount":1945,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"family-and-character","title":"家庭与品格","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/life-and-times/the-street-philosopher/family-and-character","wordCount":1855,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<p>本章呈现苏格拉底作为&quot;街头哲人&quot;的独特形象。他没有学园与著作，而是在雅典的广场、街道、作坊中，以对话的方式追求智慧；他将哲学植根于日常生活，使之成为一种生活方式。本章还描绘苏格拉底的家庭与品格——他的妻儿、独特的相貌、非凡的自制与坚韧、以及平和而幽默的性情，还原一个真实而亲切的苏格拉底。</p>\n"}